Lab
Run the Module 1 student lab, then submit a short interpretation in which every figure is accompanied by:

what changed;
what did not change;
why the change occurred; and
whether a biological conclusion would change.

By the end of this module, you should be able to:

derive and interpret nCount_RNA, nFeature_RNA, mitochondrial percentage, ribosomal percentage, and a library-complexity summary;
distinguish low-quality/dying profiles, stressed cells, empty droplets, ambient contamination, and doublets conceptually;
visualize QC distributions by cell and by sample;
explain why universal thresholds are inappropriate;
compare permissive, moderate, and aggressive filtering while changing only the QC rules;
quantify which controlled populations are preferentially lost; and
demonstrate how QC choices alter PCA structure and graph clusters.

Suggested time: 75–90 minutes of conceptual work plus 120 minutes of computation.

